{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-001","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 3","quote_original":"We say consciousness in action is imagination.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-002","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 4","quote_original":"We distinguish between the individual identity and the state of consciousness that it occupies.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-003","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 4","quote_original":"The real you is the imaginative you.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-004","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 5","quote_original":"The state from which a man observes the world determines the world that man describes.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-005","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 7","quote_original":"You will continue to see the world as you now see it, unless you change your state of consciousness.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-006","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 16","quote_original":"You are free to choose the state into which you will go.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-007","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 18","quote_original":"If you now know the world you would see had you achieved your aim, then that is the world you must begin to see in the mind’s eye.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-008","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 19","quote_original":"One that I want to stress throughout the entire series is the wide difference between thinking from an end and thinking of an end.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-009","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 25","quote_original":"I call it my wonderful imagination, and it assumes the form of all that I accept and consent to as true.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-010","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 26","quote_original":"So I set myself to observe myself and to watch how my imagination works.","primary_topic":"ATTENTION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-011","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 29","quote_original":"Learn to become aware at any moment of time of your fulfilled desire. Assume the feeling of your wish fulfilled and learn to become intensely aware of the state fulfilled, that you may look upon your world and describe it relative to your fulfilled desire.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"POA53-CUR-012","corpus_id":"L0185","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Power Of Awareness","source_year":1953,"work_class":"LECTURE","source_slug":"the_power_of_awareness","source_section":"Paragraph 32","quote_original":"I will listen as though I heard what I want to hear. I will look as though I am seeing what I want to see.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_power_of_awareness.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
